                <pb facs="0235" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg139"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Outside of Pekin murders and persecutions by Boxers increasing. Paotingfu railway
                    temporarily abandoned. Work on Pekin-Hankow line stopped. All foreigners fled.
                    Chinese Government can not or will not suppress. Troops do not attack Boxers.
                    Relations between the factions of imperial advisers very much strained. General
                    situation very critical.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
